  "limits": [
    "The fast model prices one matching contiguous BF16 copy using median measured large output-copy payload GB/s. Full-copy sensitivity interpolates whole device copy medians, including startup, using a larger 983040-byte graph copy for the 49152-byte T24 intermediate. Neither is a hardware bound. Gap, actual output copy and typed tensor work are accounted separately. Direct output assumes legal writes to the original consumer buffer and no additional alias readers.",
    "Overlap is a sensitivity on remaining work after removing intermediate traffic. Clamp by the combined direct OA+OB MAC floor at reference 1.8GHz. Splits need independently ready rounded BF16 tiles, resources and the original per-output reduction order. Credit no HCCL time, OA algorithm substitution, weight placement, or benefit of changing arithmetic. Producer-kernel initialization is unpriced; the additional per-site threshold covers it. Estimates assume full transmission through each TP join up to the historical next EP16 gate.",
    "Shape table pools matching eager sites from both collections; counts describe archive coverage only. The frozen calculation uses the singular four-wave schedule. The archived short eager pad costs are not credited to the frozen C8 or ordinary estimates.",
    "Two eager exports are used as shape references and one C8 eager history as the request schedule. Empty M416 DP1 has a positively bound zero producer, then its actual ReduceScatter. Clean 15/20-row suffixes require retaining positive zero in padded rows and original HCCL order. Neither short eager branch occurs in the C8 charged pairs. Ordinary uses the observed eager carrier times eight, interpolated stage medians, and a full graph per verification. No ordinary per-operator trace, cache state or traffic weights are inferred.",
    "64 matched forty-layer T24 rank-windows supply median per-replay costs. Multiplication uses live frozen C8 waves up to each actual endpoint; no warmup or parallel TP/DP duplication. The native source omits some eager waiting dependencies. Pipeline ceilings assume no new barriers, communication or spills; genuine physical capacity and native fused service speedups remain unverified.",
    "The unscaled BF16 single-group legacy CP route is priced. Multi-group, quantized/scaled, alternative hardware, TP1, gathered weights and optional output bank selection need their own shapes, readers and value. The factorized computation retains both GEMMs. In 15/63 prior comparisons replacing the OA primitive with plain mm had finite bit mismatches."
  ],
